    "narrative": "For the May 7th slate, **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez** headline our offensive output, both benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against Woods Richardson (xERA 4.85). **Brady House** is our strongest play of the day with a 63.81 efficiency score, buoyed by a robust platoon advantage and a premium #5 spot in the order. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** provides excellent value at 62.09; while his #9 lineup spot traditionally drags down scoring, the combination of a weak opposing arm and park factors keeps him well above our \"Strong\" start threshold. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start at 69.76; despite facing a tougher arm in Meyer, his leadoff placement and positive platoon dynamics make him our most potent engine for R and SB production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Coby Mayo**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 38.03. While **Coby Mayo** has the raw power profile we covet, the combination of facing Meyer\u2019s 3.69 xERA and a lowly #8 spot in the batting order pushed him just below our 40.0 floor. Elsewhere, **Jackson Merrill** is a high-upside play at 59.87; he sits right on the edge of \"Strong\" status, though his score remains sensitive to his \"Lineup Pending\" status as we await confirmation of his spot against the lefty Liberatore. **Liam Hicks** rounds out the lineup at 42.14, representing a marginal start necessitated by the need to manage our long-term game caps, as his dynamic platoon disadvantage against Povich keeps his ceiling capped for today\u2019s contest.",
